.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-ATTACH" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-attach - Attach or detach an explicitly selected personal resource


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team attach <team> <preview|tunnel> <resource> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Attach or detach an explicitly selected personal resource

.PP
Attach or detach an exact personal preview or tunnel to a team. --generation guards against stale changes, and --active chooses the desired attachment state.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant device use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--active\fP[=true]
	attach resource; set false to detach

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for attach

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
